 ### Claude Code sessions
 
+New sessions run on your Claude subscription (the Claude Code harness) by default:
+`[sessions].default_harness = "claude_code"`. If the `claude` CLI isn't installed they use the
+built-in loop. Scheduled tasks, campaigns, fleet and subagents keep the built-in loop, existing
+sessions keep their harness, and workflows aren't offered in Claude subscription sessions (they need
+the built-in loop with an API key).
+
 Checked against claude 2.1.308 logged in with a claude.ai subscription: login detection, the
 stream-json protocol, the PreToolUse hook, the permission prompt tool, GDW's MCP tools, Plan mode's
 plan card, questions, Stop and `--resume` (redacted captures in `tests/fixtures/claude_stream/`).
